  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Alkyl aryl ethers are cleaved at the alkyl-oxygen bond due to the more stable aryl-oxygen bond. The reaction yields phenol and alkyl halide.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/12f37d8a-5472-411d-99fc-05d5d72cd52e-9758467_S.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 113px;\" /></p><p>And then&nbsp;Phenol is converted to benzene on heating with zinc dust.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/77a292b5-64f2-473f-b797-ad195fc9a9b7-image.png\" style=\"width: 538px; height: 80px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
